          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Principle and Config",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Test what the user sees and does==, not component internals",
                "The more tests resemble **real usage**, the more confidence they give",
                "Config goes in `vite.config` or `vitest.config`",
                "`setupTests.ts`: `import '@testing-library/jest-dom/vitest'` adds `toBeInTheDocument`, `toBeDisabled`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "typescript",
              "lines": [
                "export default defineConfig({",
                "  test: {",
                "    environment: 'jsdom',",
                "    globals: true,",
                "    setupFiles: './src/setupTests.ts',",
                "  },",
                "})"
              ],
              "note": "vitest config"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Render and Cleanup",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`render(<App />)` mounts into ==document.body==",
                "`screen` queries the **whole document**",
                "Auto-cleanup after each test only when {green:globals: true}",
                "Otherwise call `cleanup` in `afterEach`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Vitest vs Jest",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Jest",
                "Vitest"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`jest.fn()`",
                  "`vi.fn()`"
                ],
                [
                  "`jest.mock()`",
                  "`vi.mock()`"
                ],
                [
                  "`jest.spyOn()`",
                  "`vi.spyOn()`"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Hoisting",
              "text": "`vi.mock` is ==hoisted to the top of the file==, above your imports."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
