    {
      "title": "user-event and Async Assertions",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "user-event and Async Assertions",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Setup and Core Calls",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`userEvent.setup()` ==before== `render`",
                "Every call is **async**: always `await user.click(el)`"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "tsx",
              "lines": [
                "const user = userEvent.setup()",
                "render(<Form />)",
                "await user.type(input, 'hello')",
                "await user.clear(input)",
                "await user.selectOptions(select, 'a')",
                "await user.keyboard('{Enter}')",
                "await user.tab()",
                "await user.click(btn)"
              ],
              "note": "setup first, then render"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. user-event vs fireEvent",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "user-event",
                "fireEvent"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Events",
                  "hover, focus, keydown, keyup, input",
                  "one raw DOM event"
                ],
                [
                  "Mimics",
                  "a real {green:user}",
                  "just the {red:event}"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Async Assertions",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`await screen.findByText('Saved')` = ==waitFor + getByText==",
                "Use it when the element appears after **async work**",
                "`waitFor` retries the callback until it ==passes== or times out",
                "Keep ==one assertion== inside it",
                "Disappearing spinner: `waitForElementToBeRemoved`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "tsx",
              "lines": [
                "await screen.findByText('Saved')",
                "await waitFor(() => expect(spy).toHaveBeenCalled())",
                "await waitForElementToBeRemoved(",
                "  () => screen.queryByText('Loading'))"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Common mistakes",
              "text": "A missing `await` runs the assertion ==too early==. A click inside `waitFor` **repeats** on every retry."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Mocking fetch with MSW",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Mocking fetch with MSW",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Why MSW",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==MSW== intercepts at the **network level**",
                "Component code calls the {green:real fetch}, unchanged",
                "Beats mocking `fetch` itself: no stubs tied to call shape"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Handlers and Lifecycle",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "import { http, HttpResponse } from 'msw'",
                "import { setupServer } from 'msw/node'",
                "const server = setupServer(",
                "  http.get('/api/users', () => HttpResponse.json([{ id: 1 }])))",
                "beforeAll(() => server.listen({ onUnhandledRequest: 'error' }))",
                "afterEach(() => server.resetHandlers())",
                "afterAll(() => server.close())"
              ],
              "note": "listen once, reset each test, close at the end"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "v1 (old)",
                "v2 (current)"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Route",
                  "`rest.get`",
                  "`http.get`"
                ],
                [
                  "Reply",
                  "`res(ctx.json())`",
                  "`HttpResponse.json()`"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Overrides and Gotchas",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "server.use(",
                "  http.get('/api/users', () =>",
                "    new HttpResponse(null, { status: 500 })))"
              ],
              "note": "per-test error state; resetHandlers restores defaults"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Relative URL in jsdom: needs a base, or use ==absolute URLs== in handlers",
                "Node below 18 has no `fetch`: request never reaches MSW"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Reset every test",
              "text": "Without `afterEach` ==resetHandlers==, one test's `server.use` override leaks into the next."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Testing Hooks and Avoiding Implementation Details",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Testing Hooks and Avoiding Implementation Details",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. renderHook Basics",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`renderHook(() => useCounter(0))` returns `{ result, rerender, unmount }`",
                "Read the latest value from ==result.current==",
                "Wrap state changes in ==act()== so React flushes before you assert"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "const { result } = renderHook(() => useCounter(0))",
                "act(() => {",
                "  result.current.increment()",
                "})",
                "expect(result.current.count).toBe(1)"
              ],
              "note": "assert after act, never before"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Context and Changing Props",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "const { result, rerender } = renderHook(",
                "  ({ id }) => useUser(id),",
                "  { initialProps: { id: 1 }, wrapper: AuthProvider }",
                ")",
                "rerender({ id: 2 })"
              ],
              "note": "wrapper supplies context, rerender passes new props"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Hook is",
                "Test it with"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Used by **one** component",
                  "Render that component, assert what the user sees"
                ],
                [
                  "Reusable, own contract",
                  "`renderHook` directly"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Avoid Implementation Details",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Asserting on state values",
                "Calling instance methods",
                "Snapshot-testing whole trees",
                "Shallow rendering",
                "Querying by CSS class or test id"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Assert behavior",
              "text": "Check ==visible text==, ==roles== and behavior, so a refactor does not break the tests."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
